{"resource": {"name": "County Sheriff Reported Crimes", "id": "ahxi-5nsc", "resource_name": null, "parent_fxf": [], "description": "Reported crimes of the Marin County Sheriff's Department. Data is updated every four hours. Data begins as of January 1, 2013. Each reported crime includes its date/time, approximate location, crime type, and crime classification.\r\n\r\nNOTE: For the safety and security of victims of crimes, street address locations, other than reported street intersections or highway locations, are not exact.  They are adjusted to the nearest block level.\r\n\r\nThere are two columns of city/town information.  The first is the reported city/town name in the crime records.  The second, which is not in the crime records, is a translation of it into the more commonly known city/town name, or into Marin County when it appears to be in an unincorporated area.  For example, Almonte and Tam Valley are reported city/town names, but they are both in the more commonly known city of Mill Valley.  Lucas Valley translates to San Rafael, etc.  We hope that the translated city/town column will facilitate analysis.", "attribution": "County of Marin, CA", "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2024-11-03T07:05:03.000Z", "createdAt": "2017-04-20T16:46:08.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2024-06-18T21:39:44.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2024-11-03T07:05:03.000Z", "columns_name": ["Supervisor District Shapefile", "Park Boundary Shapefile", "Elementary School District Shapefile", "Longitude", "City Shapefile", "Crime City Town Region", "Crime City Town Reported", "Crime Class", "Case Number", "Crime Time", "Crime Street Highway", "Latitude", "Crime", "location (address)", "location (zip)", "location (city)", "Police Jurisdiction", "location (state)", "Location", "City Community Shape File dataset", "Zip Code", "Unique ID"], "columns_field_name": [":@computed_region_nyxm_p3bi", ":@computed_region_yigg_54f9", ":@computed_region_bgqc_3ap